E4-S4B PRE-REGISTRATION -- written 2026-10-10 before any E4-S4B run; hash in e4_s4b_preregistration.sha256.
Task: docs/memory/handoffs/E4-S4B_GRAB_DEFERRAL_CLEAN_LINK_TASK.md under QUEUE_2026-10-10B.md (every standing rule;
E3-A3B's validity reading; E4-S2's constraint discipline). Baseline: 7331184 plus the uncommitted E4-S1..S5 work
(untouched; E4-S3B's / E4-S5B's files and E4-S3B's runner patch beside it). References: E4-S1 (e4_s1_2026-10-09/),
E4-S2 (e4_s2_2026-10-09/), E4-S4 (e4_s4_2026-10-10/: its pre-registration, bar and pass-rule copy).

0. THE CHANGE, E4-S4's, unchanged (e4_s4_2026-10-10/e4_s4_change.diff; companion/plugins/epg.py sha256 __EPG_SHA__):
   behind PRIVYHUB_EPG_DEFER_WHILE_STREAMING=1, a forced grab while a stream session is live is queued and answered
   with the cached guide marked refresh_deferred; the queue drains when the session ends. The runner (tools/e1_suite.py
   sha256 __SUITE_SHA__ -- E4-S3B's back-off patch included; answered calls take E4-S4's path unchanged): the deferred
   row + 5-s wait, the teardown's drain wait and record. The flag lives in e3_flag.conf for its runs only.
   Driver: e4_s4b_run.py sha256 __RUN_SHA__.

1. THE CLEAN-LINK GATE (the only addition): THE CONTROL, E1-PS1-STREAM x1, no flag (tools/e1_suite.py run --e2 --window
   1200 --gap 120, E2's warm-up), runs first. It is CLEAN if its video loss/min < 10 (D-BASE's row) AND rendered fps
   >= 59.5 AND resyncs <= 10. If not clean: idle 30 min, run the control again -- up to 4 controls. The first clean
   control is THE control; the flagged runs start after it. If none of the four is clean: INCONCLUSIVE (link), no
   flagged run, the four controls' figures in the record, and the task ends there. (A control that never reaches
   PLAYING after the runner's two replacements counts as a not-clean attempt.)

2. THE RUNS after a clean control, E2's windows and gaps, exactly E4-S4's: E1-CONC x2 with the flag (unconstrained;
   runs/E1-CONC_flag/run1, run2), E1-CONC x1 with the flag at CPUQuota=150% (runs/E1-CONC_flag_cpu150/run1; the drop-in
   e4_constraint.conf as E4-S2: written, read back, removed at teardown, properties read back infinity / max), one
   suite invocation. Each CONC teardown waits for the deferred queue to drain (<= 600 s) and records it.
   THE PRE-RUN GUIDE READ (tools/e1_suite.py guide_read, the six channels, non-forced) is taken 60 s after the clean
   control's teardown, immediately before the flagged runs (not before the first control as in E4-S4: the gate may
   span hours and the guide's programme totals move with the clock) -> pre_guide.json.

3. COMPARABILITY (else INCONCLUSIVE): the control within E1's bands of E4-S1's PS1-STREAM: host CPU 10.9 +/- 2;
   rendered fps 59.53 +/- 0.5.

4. THE BAR = E4-S4's, verbatim (e4_s4_preregistration.txt §3) -- ACCEPTED only if all hold; REJECTED if any fails
   (comparability holding):
   (a) CONC with the flag, BOTH unconstrained runs: video loss/min <= 3 x the control's AND <= 100; rendered fps
       >= 59.5; resyncs <= 10; host CPU within +/- 2 points of the control's;
   (b) the deferral did what it says, in each of the three CONC runs: 0 grabber processes during the window (no
       sampler row with an EPG child, samples.jsonl procs.epg); the queue grew (epg.jsonl "deferred" rows with pending
       rising to the six channels); after teardown the queue drained with failed 0 and pending 0, every queued channel
       refreshed (drained ok = queued), within 2 x the cycle's normal time for that many grabs (E4-S1 CONC's median
       grab 5.3 s: 2 x 5.3 x the count; 63.6 s for six);
   (c) the guide serves after each drain: all six channels serve, programmes total within +/- 5 % of the pre-run read;
   (d) CONC with the flag at CPUQuota=150% passes E4-S2's pass rule as a stream row (rendered >= 59.5, RetroArch
       >= 59.9, capture 60 +/- 0.5 segment-aware, dup+drop <= 0.2/min, spikes < 200, stale < 20; grabs failed 0 is
       vacuous here; the link-INCONCLUSIVE clause as E4-S2 with THIS task's control), its throttled time reported;
   (e) the companion's CPU (% of a core) in each unconstrained CONC run within +/- 2 points of the control's.
   (The analysis is e4_s4_analysis.py's, copied as e4_s4b_analysis.py with THE control taken from the gate; the pass
   rule e4_s4_passrule.py copied byte for byte as e4_s4b_passrule.py, one comment line added.)
   REPORTED: cap_fired (expected 0), the drain times, the client's pauses, the gap log, socket W, the deferred rows per
   window; and -- if a flagged run's link goes bad mid-night (loss > 3 x the clean control's) -- that it did, with the
   host-side clauses (b), (c), (e) and (d)'s host gates stated on their own, so the record says which clause the link
   took.

5. WHAT ADOPTION WOULD MEAN (stated in the record, the user's call): E4-S2 §5's table with the deferral line -- the
   stack's CPU-time floor PS1-STREAM's 150 %, 4 cores; the one-line adoption, a drop-in epg-defer.conf,
